      "width": 427,
      "height": 640,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0",
      "artist": "Chris Allen",
      "description": "Derby Industrial Museum - gates. Fine gates by Robert Bakewell that used to be across the bridge crossing the tail race and barred entry to Lombe's silk mill. This position is close to the original but to one side and perpendicular. The low cover beyond is over the parts of the steam winding engine from Morton Colliery (I thought this had long since been scrapped). Beyond that the arched window is the end of the gallery housing a Rolls-Royce RB211 engine.",
      "dateCreated": "2011-01-29",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "derby-silk-mill-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "gcqv"
    },
